From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] the NTSC rate from the exact master clock, not a rounded one

The NTSC frame rate came from a master clock rounded to 21477272 Hz. The
SNES's is 945/44 MHz = 21477272.727..., six times the NTSC subcarrier -
the value the emulator itself runs at (Colorburst::NTSC * 6) - and the
rounding leaves the reported rate 0.034 ppm low.

The panel mode this core selects is cut to twice the exact rate,
120.197628 Hz. Against the rounded clock it is +0.037 ppm, a frame of
drift every 63 hours; against the exact one +0.003 ppm, every 824.

--- a/bsnes/target-libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/bsnes/target-libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -775,7 +775,10 @@ void retro_get_system_av_info(struct retro_system_av_info *info)
 	info->timing.sample_rate   = SAMPLERATE;
 
 	if (retro_get_region() == RETRO_REGION_NTSC) {
-		info->timing.fps = 21477272.0 / 357366.0;
+		// 945/44 MHz, six times the colour subcarrier, over 357366 master
+		// clocks a frame. 21477272 rounds it 0.034 ppm low, enough to miss
+		// a panel mode cut to twice the true rate.
+		info->timing.fps = Emulator::Constants::Colorburst::NTSC * 6.0 / 357366.0;
 		audio_buffer_max = (SAMPLERATE/60) * 2;
 	}
 	else
